The '''third series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began airing on Tuesday 14 August 2012.<ref>{{citation |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/mediapacks/food/ |title=Food on BBC Two |date=26 April 2012}}</ref> The series was filmed at [[Harptree Court]] in [[East Harptree]], Somerset.

Seven thousand applied for the competition and twelve contestants were chosen.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.lichfieldpeople.co.uk/Stuart-beats-7-000-hopefuls-join-TV-Bake-dozen/story-16680166-detail/story.html |title= 'Sir' beat 7,000 hopefuls to join baking dozen |work=Lichfield Mercury |date=9 August 2012}}</ref> The competition was won by [[John Whaite]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Great British Bake Off: John Whaite is surprise winner|url= https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2012/oct/16/great-british-bake-off-john-whaite|author=Vicky Frost |work=The Guardian |date=16 October 2012}}</ref>

The third series was broadcast as the fifth season on [[PBS]] in the United States.

