===Extras and special episodes (Episodes 11–14)===
Four additional episodes were broadcast after the final. 
*Episode 11 was a masterclass by Paul and Mary where they demonstrated how to make the technical challenges they set – treacle tarts, rum babas, creme caramels, the hand-raised pie, and the eight-strand plaited loaf. 
*Episode 12 revisited the bakers from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 2)|series two]] to catch up on what these contestants had been doing after the show ended. 
*Another masterclass was shown in episode 13 where Paul and Mary showed how to make Queen of Puddings, jam doughnuts, tempered chocolate teacakes, Fraisier cakes and fondant fancies. 
*In episode 14, Paul and Mary showed which signature bakes they would have chosen if they were in the bakers' shoes (including sponge puddings, flat breads and sweet buns). Two further episodes of Masterclass were shown, one before Christmas and another before Easter.

==Post-show career==

[[John Whaite]] gained a first-class degree from the [[University of Manchester]] after sitting his law exams while filming Bake Off, but he rejected a career in law and opted to take classes at [[Le Cordon Bleu]] and pursue a career in baking.{{citation needed|date=April 2020}} His book ''John Whaite Bakes: Recipes for Every Day and Every Mood'' was published on 25 April 2013.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://uk.lifestyle.yahoo.com/great-british-bake-off-john-whaite-depression-battle--151116798.html |title=John Whaite: How baking helps me battle depression – EXCLUSIVE |author=Sophia Moir | work=Yahoo Lifestyle |date=26 April 2013}}</ref> His second book, ''John Whaite Bakes at Home'', was published on 27 March 2014.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.mancunianmatters.co.uk/content/270368308-winner-bakes-it-all-great-british-bake-ace-john-whaite-reveals-guilty-secrets-and |title=The winner bakes it all: Great British Bake Off ace John Whaite reveals guilty secrets and making mum jealous |date=27 March 2014 |author=Josh Willacy |work=Mancunian Matters}}</ref> He first set up a chocolate shop The Hungry Dog Artisan Chocolates,<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.iol.co.za/tonight/tv-radio/whaite-s-victory-tastes-extra-sweet-1.1717487 |title=Whaite's victory tastes extra sweet |date=10 July 2014 |author=Debashine Thangevelo|work=Tonight}}</ref> and opened a cookery school on his family's dairy farm in Lancashire.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-what-past-winners-are-doing-now-from-edd-kimber-to-last-years-frances-quinn-9780390.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-what-past-winners-are-doing-now-from-edd-kimber-to-last-years-frances-quinn-9780390.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off 2014: What past winners are doing now from Edd Kimber to last year's Frances Quinn |author=Jess Denham |date=7 October 2014 |work=The Independent}}</ref> He also appeared as a resident chef on the ITV show [[Lorraine (TV programme)|Lorraine]],<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11012728/Bake-Off-the-winners-reveal-their-secrets.html |title=Bake Off: the winners reveal their secrets |author=Helena Kealey |date=5 August 2014 |work=The Daily Telegraph}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.itv.com/lorraine/john-whaite |title=John Whaite |work=ITV}}</ref> and wrote a column on food for ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/journalists/john-whaite/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150316134500/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/journalists/john-whaite/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=2015-03-16 |title=John Whaite |work=The Daily Telegraph}}</ref> In 2016, Whaite presented with [[Rosemary Shrager]] a daytime cookery competitive show ''Chopping Block'' on ITV.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.itv.com/presscentre/press-packs/chopping-block |title= Chopping Block |date=24 March 2016}}</ref> In 2018, after six years of directing his attention on writing cookbooks, leading baking classes, and making television appearances, Whaite decided to refocus on law.<ref>{{Cite web|date=22 July 2018|title=Former Great British Bake Off winner John Whaite returning to law "to devote myself to something utterly important"|url=https://inews.co.uk/inews-lifestyle/food-and-drink/great-british-bake-off-gbbo-john-whaite-season-three-solicitor-legal-179237|access-date=2020-06-18|website=inews.co.uk|language=en}}</ref>

James Morton aimed for a career in medicine but has written a book on bread, titled ''Brilliant Bread'', published on 29 August 2013.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/entertainment/celebrity-interviews/great-british-bake-star-james-1546478 |author= Heather Greenaway |title= Great British Bake Off star James Morton: Cooking is great.. but my real dream is to be a doctor |work= Daily Record |date= 20 January 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url= http://www.edinburghfoody.com/2013/07/19/james-and-the-world-bread-awards/ |title= James and the World Bread Awards |work= Edinburgh Foody |date=19 July 2013}}</ref> He writes a baking column for the Scottish newspaper ''[[Sunday Mail (Scotland)|Sunday Mail]]''.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/all-about/james-morton |title= Jame Mortan |work= Daily Record and Sunday Mail}}</ref> His second book, ''How Baking Works: ...And what to do if it doesn't'', was published on 12 March 2015.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.independent.co.uk/extras/indybest/10-best-cookbooks-by-great-british-bake-off-contestants-james-morton-ruby-tandoh-a6680291.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/extras/indybest/10-best-cookbooks-by-great-british-bake-off-contestants-james-morton-ruby-tandoh-a6680291.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title= Great British Bake Off: 10 best cookbooks |author= Pippa Bailey Monday |date= 5 October 2015 |work= The Independent}}</ref> He later participated in both the 2016 and 2024 renditions of ''The Great New Year's Bake Off''.

Brendan Lynch is teaching cookery classes.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.express.co.uk/news/health/386513/Baking-an-end-to-the-lonely-days |title= Baking an end to the lonely days |work=Daily Express |author= Giulia Rhodes |date= 24 March 2013 |accessdate=31 March 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url= http://www.uttoxeter-news.co.uk/Bake-finalist-join-Seasoned-Cookery-School/story-21616449-detail/story.html |title= Bake off finalist to join Seasoned Cookery School |author= James Brindle |work= Uttoxeter Advertiser |date=25 October 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/whats-on/great-british-bake-off-contestants-7545213 |title= Whatever happened to the 'Great British Bake Off' bakers from the Midlands? |date=2 August 2014 |author= Roz Laws |work= Birmingham Mail}}</ref>

Cathryn Dresser and Sarah-Jane Willis teamed up to open a stall at [[Horsham]] Market.<ref>{{cite news |url= http://www.theargus.co.uk/news/10001479.Crawley_Bake_Off_stars_set_up_own_business/ |title= Crawley Bake Off stars set up own business |work=The Argus |date= 23 October 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url= http://www.crawleyobserver.co.uk/news/videos/tv-bake-off-stars-team-up-to-run-market-stall-1-4426151 |title= TV Bake-off stars team up to run market stall |work= Crawley and Horley Observer |date= 31 October 2012}}</ref> Dresser wrote a baking book for children and parents titled ''Let's Bake'', published on 22 May 2014.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.welovethisbook.com/features/review-lets-bake-cathryn-dresser|title=REVIEW: LET'S BAKE BY CATHRYN DRESSER|author=Anna James|work=We Love This Book|date=20 May 2014|access-date=2 August 2014|archive-date=8 August 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140808053357/http://www.welovethisbook.com/features/review-lets-bake-cathryn-dresser|url-status=dead}}</ref> and ran ''The Little Handcross Bakery''<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.midsussextimes.co.uk/news/local/hectic-life-of-a-mother-and-celebrity-baker-1-6318151 |title=Hectic life of a mother and celebrity baker}}</ref> in [[Handcross]], West Sussex between September 2014 and May 2015. Dresser later participated in the 2016 rendition of ''The Great Christmas Bake Off''.

